@CloudOps_Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5286

### Get all incidents
GET {{CloudOps_Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents
Accept: application/json

###

### Get incident #1
GET {{CloudOps_Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/1
Accept: application/json

###

### Create a new incident
POST {{CloudOps_Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Azure application health alert",
  "description": "Application health monitoring detected elevated response times.",
  "severity": "High",
  "status": "Open",
  "assignedTo": "Platform Engineering"
}

###

### Update incident #1
PUT {{CloudOps_Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Production API unavailable",
  "description": "The customer API experienced HTTP 503 errors.",
  "severity": "Critical",
  "status": "Resolved",
  "assignedTo": "Cloud Operations",
  "resolvedAt": "2026-09-21T13:00:00Z",
  "resolutionNotes": "Application service was restarted and API health checks returned to normal."
}

###

### Delete incident #2
DELETE {{CloudOps_Api_HostAddress}}/api/incidents/2